    "source": "SANS DataFinder Keywords.csv",
    "description": "Structured, enriched version of the raw keyword CSV used as input to the scraping pipeline. Each entry has two kinds of local match terms: 'search_terms' (exact word/phrase, word-boundary matched) and 'stems' (word-initial prefix matched, e.g. stem 'empath' matches empathy/empathic/empathize/empathetic) -- stems are only used for terms that are long/unique enough to be low-risk; short or generic words are kept exact-only. Both are also used verbatim (search_terms quoted, stems as 'stem*' wildcards) to build the Europe PMC discovery query. 'schema_topics' / 'schema_modality' map an entry onto the controlled vocabularies in data/schema.json; an empty mapping means the label has no clean existing enum match, so matches are stored in 'tags' instead until a 'propose vocabulary' PR adds it."
  },
